{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "measuredDate": "2026-10-03",
  "conclusion": "The shared home upstream path is a demonstrated constraint near 5.3 Mbps of available payload throughput even when Funnel is bypassed. Exact ISP/router/congestion cause and a higher Funnel ceiling remain unmeasured.",
  "topology": "Personal Windows PC remains the only local test backend. Mac is a client on the same home LAN using its existing VPN, with a verified different IPv4 Internet exit.",
  "cloudflareSource": "https://github.com/cloudflare/speedtest",
  "sourceSHA256": {
    "initialWan": "999765da68eee07309a7015ca32b55235a74101833e7cbcdaf8a19c24655dac1",
    "ipv4Wan": "43149fda71c7831cb1aee9b36076f6d0436c9f87961a783da775a7edb53772da",
    "funnel": "e9a58d63bf3831ff15d610ed9504144914fa18441b24cf9e011763bbc797e47f"
  },
  "methodology": [
    "WAN rates count known payload bytes through a completed transfer including setup/response time; upload API has no exact byte-count echo.",
    "Original WAN controls use default IP-family selection; explicit IPv4 uploads and simultaneous IPv4 uploads provide the like-for-like Funnel control.",
    "Mixed WAN aggregate counts both payloads over the full coordinator wall time, including SSH/process overhead.",
    "Funnel goodput requires complete integrity checks and final byte acknowledgement.",
    "Parallel Funnel aggregate uses all verified bytes over the union of actual receiver intervals; it does not sum per-flow average rates.",
    "Overlap lower bounds use only cumulative sample differences fully inside the shared receiving window, excluding ambiguous boundary bytes."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Mac shares the physical home WAN and is not a fully independent off-site host.",
    "No router/ISP configuration or competing-household-traffic counters were inspected; these tests do not identify an ISP plan or a specific shaper.",
    "An additional Funnel-specific limit is not excluded; its capacity above the constrained upstream path is unknown.",
    "No complete phone/cellular or production Mobile Egress protocol throughput was measured."
  ],
